<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangeran Dipati Anta-Kasuma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangeran Dipati Anta-Kasuma was the founder and first ruler of the Kotawaringin Sultanate in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, established in the early 17th century. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mustain Billah of Banjar, he was given the western lands of the Banjar realm to rule. His descendants governed Kotawaringin first under Banjar and later under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> suzerainty.</p></div>
